:name: RA4M1 HAL analog smoke (ADC14 + DAC12)
:description: Boots the real ra4m1-hal `analog` example ELF on the UNO R4 Minima
:             platform with the GPT320 time base plus the custom ADC14/DAC12
:             models, so the async ADC scan-complete -> DAC-mirror chain runs.
:
: Run headless from the REPO ROOT (paths are repo-relative; Renode's monitor
: cannot tokenize the spaces/parens some checkout paths contain, so keep the
: working directory at the repo root and use relative @paths):
:
:   cd <repo-root>
:   cargo build --release -p ra4m1-hal --example analog \
:     --target thumbv7em-none-eabihf
:   <renode-install>/renode --console --disable-xwt --plain \
:     -e 'include @renode/analog.resc' \
:     -e 'start'
:
: Observe (see renode/analog.robot for the automated pass/fail):
:   DAC DADR (mirror of A0 >> 2): sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x4005E000
:   DAC DAOE0 (output enabled)  : sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x4005E004  (bit 6)
:   ADC ADDR0 (raw A0 sample)   : sysbus ReadWord 0x4005C020

$elf ?= @target/thumbv7em-none-eabihf/release/examples/analog

# Compile the custom models BEFORE any platform description references them.
# Ra4m1Gpt320 is required by the base platform (the time base); the ADC/DAC
# models are bound by the fragment below.
include @renode/Ra4m1Gpt320.cs
include @renode/Ra4m1Dac.cs
include @renode/Ra4m1Adc.cs

mach create "uno-r4-analog"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @renode/ra4m1-uno-r4.repl

# Attach the ADC14 + DAC12 models on top of the base platform, where the stock
# repl has only absorbing Tags.  ADC scan-complete (S12ADI0) -> ICU event 0x29
# via the inline connection block, mirroring the driver's SCAN_END_EVENT
# (adc.rs) and the base platform's gpt0 -> icu@0x57 idiom.  Registering a real
# peripheral over the stock Tag range is fine — the peripheral takes precedence;
# the Tag only names otherwise-unhandled accesses.
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString "adc: Analog.Ra4m1Adc @ sysbus 0x4005c000 { 0 -> icu@0x29 }"
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString "dac: Analog.Ra4m1Dac @ sysbus 0x4005e000"

sysbus LoadELF $elf

# This script only builds the machine; issue `start` (or `emulation RunFor`)
# after including it so the caller controls a deterministic, bounded run.
